        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "997d2ac0-f2f1-51f6-ad36-5406132a98bd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Masahiko Takeshita, Kenji Hatanaka, Yoshihiro Tokugawa, Tokugawa Yoshikatsu\n- Roles: Emperor of Japan, Grand Chamberlain of Japan\n- Organizations: Imperial Family\n- Places: Japan\n- Events: Japan's surrender, August 1945 coup plot\n\nFacts:\n- In August 1945, Masahiko Takeshita helped plan a coup with Major Kenji Hatanaka and several others to prevent the Emperor of Japan's announcement of Japan's surrender from being broadcast.\n- The Emperor of Japan is the head of the Imperial Family and the traditional head of state of Japan.\n- Yoshihiro Tokugawa was the grandson of Tokugawa Yoshikatsu, the last lord of Owari han.\n- From 1985 to 1988, Yoshihiro Tokugawa served as Grand Chamberlain of Japan as the personal adviser to the Emperor of Japan.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
